  "description": "EVOLVED\n\nThe partnership between BH's R&D team and the BH Coloma Team has allowed us to optimise the geometry and kinematics of the Lynx Race for 120 mm of travel while maintaining excellent performance with 100 mm of travel. A slightly relaxed steering angle, a more upright seat tube, a longer reach and a lower steering tube for fully optimised geometries.\n\nLIGHTWEIGHT\n\nThe Lynx Race RC range has been built like all of BH's high-end frames; using Hollow Core Internal Moulding (HCIM) technology, allowing us to minimise the weight of the frame and the rocker link. We use high modulus carbon fibres (T1100 and T800) - Performance Carbon Lay Up - which provide outstanding lightness and stiffness for the frame.\n\n+ STIFFNESS\n\nThe stiffness of the joint between the rear triangle and swingarm has been improved by 35% on the new Lynx Race, thanks to the new spindle design on the rocker link and the oversized main pivot axle.\n\nOUTSTANDING PEDALLING EFFICIENCY\n\nGuaranteed by the Spilt Pivot suspension system that ensures: Outstanding pedalling efficiency without the open position of the shock absorber interfering with pedalling, resulting in better traction and making optimal use of your energy.\n\n2 BOTTLES\n\nOne in its usual place on the down tube and one on the seat tube, using a small adaptor to ensure an optimal position.",
